Allow DOH's broker placeholder through sandbox env scrubbing.

Hermes Agent intentionally strips provider credentials (GITHUB_TOKEN, etc.)
from terminal / execute_code children and rejects terminal.env_passthrough for
those names (GHSA-rhgp-j443-p4rf). DOH's integrations broker, however, only
ever surfaces the literal placeholder DOH_PLACEHOLDER to child processes; it
swaps that placeholder for the connected user's short-lived token on the wire.

The placeholder is non-secret by construction, so gate on the *value* rather
than a fixed list of variable names: any env var whose value is exactly
DOH_PLACEHOLDER passes through, regardless of name. Real credentials never
carry this value, so they stay blocked. This lets `gh`, git, and other
provider-aware tools run inside Hermes without storing user tokens in the
sandbox, and needs no edit when the set of DOH providers changes.
